we Minerals (Pty) Ltd K17 and Belmont Magnetotelluric survey Deep profile over 51 km followed by a 30 km2 grid Sept 2024 Ongwe Minerals (Pty) Ltd Belmont Diamond drilling 4 holes for 570 m Nov","year":2024},{"method":"magnetics","page":42,"text":"Source: Rompel (2023) 9.2.3 Magnetic and Imaging Survey A drone-based magnetic survey was completed in November 2024 with 1,543 line-km flown at a line spacing of 50 m and mean terrain clearance of 25 m (Figure 9-7).","platform":"airborne","year":2023,"line_km":1543.0,"line_spacing_m":50.0},{"method":"magnetics","page":48,"text":"conductors (C1-C3) outlined in white Source: Great Quest (2024b) 9.3.3 Magnetic Survey A drone-based imaging and magnetic survey covering 869 line-km was completed in early 2025, targeting structural and magnetite mapping and","year":2025,"line_km":869.0},{"method":"magnetics","page":49,"text":"Ongwe (2026) 9.3.4 Interpretation Integration of drone imagery, drone magnetic surveys, geological mapping, and rock chip data confirm that mineralization at K17 is structurally controlled.","year":2026},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":73,"text":"Geophysical work completed to date (MT, detailed magnetics, EM surveys) supports this model and has provided encouraging results for a large-scale mineralizing system at K17 and the Southern Shear."},{"method":"gravity","page":73,"text":"Geophysical work should include gravity surveys to define any underlying intrusions and/or massive alteration zones, and IP to define disseminated mineralization at depth."},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":74,"text":"Scout diamond drilling for fresh rock structural and mineralogical information.","year":2026},{"method":"gravity","page":74,"text":"Scout diamond drilling for fresh rock structural and mineralogical information.","year":2026},{"method":"magnetics","page":82,"text":"Page: 73 Glossary of Technical Terms Technical Term Description Airborne magnetic surveys Surveys flown by helicopter, fixed wing aircraft or drone to measure the magnetic susceptibility of rocks at or near the earth\u2019s surface","platform":"airborne"}],"targets":[{"page":11,"explained":false,"untested":true,"text":"NI 43-101 Technical Report Page: 2 The QP recommends a 2-phased exploration program including regional and detailed geophysical surveys (magnetics, induced polarization, gravity), testing of surface soil and calcrete geochemical anomalies through bedrock sampl"},{"page":44,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"Grab samples returned up to 16.45 g/t Au. The geochemical anomaly is coincident with a strong magnetic anomaly. The target is centred around a series of iron-oxide rich (interpreted as oxidized sulphides) quartz veins, striking roughly NW-SE."},{"page":71,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"At the K17 Prospect, surface copper-gold-silver mineralization, magnetic signatures, and MT conductors define a separate polymetallic target associated with folded and altered chloritic schists."}]},"rock":null,"model_params":{"composite_m":4.0,"default_cutoff":0.1,"metallurgy":{"routes":[],"traits":["sulphide","arsenic"],"recoveries":null,"summary":"sulphide ore, arsenic-bearing"},"deposit_style":"vein","dip_direction":180.0},"effective_date":"2026-05-31","resource":null,"resource_rows":[],"counts":{"collars":49,"intervals":51,"surveyed_holes":0,"holes_with_intervals":21,"linked":19},"collars":[{"hole":"BKP001","e":505.0,"n":740.0,"z":998.7,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":50.0},{"hole":"BKP002","e":505.0,"n":740.0,"z":998.8,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":50.0},{"hole":"BKP003","e":505.0,"n":741.0,"z":998.8,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":52.0},{"hole":"BKP004","e":505.0,"n":741.0,"z":998.9,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":50.0},{"hole":"BKP005","e":505.0,"n":741.0,"z":998.9,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":50.0},{"hole":"BKP006","e":505.0,"n":741.0,"z":999.0,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":50.0},{"hole":"BKP007","e":505.0,"n":741.0,"z":999.1,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":50.0},{"hole":"BKP008","e":505.0,"n":741.0,"z